  "body": "## What changed\n\nA machine file whose rotary C states a travel but no rate (neither its feed nor its rapid, deg/min) had nothing to cap the C rewind orbit of #860 by. The lathe post scaled the machine's max linear feed by the C turn, about 57 x fmax / r (the F22954 of the #860 review, note 1). It now refuses by name, in two layers:\n\n- **Generation** (`crates/app/src/operation/rotary_gate.rs`): when `unwind_c` inserts a rewind orbit (the path grows) and the machine's C states no rate, Rotary Contour is refused: \"the path needs a C rewind, but the machine file states a C travel but no C rate - a rewind would post at an uncapped feed; state the C axis's feed or rapid rate\". A shift of the opening stretch adds no move (the section's first G00 C positions it, at no F), so it is not refused. A path that fits the travel as stamped is not refused.\n- **Lathe post** (`assets/posts/fanuc-lathe.cps`, `liveMove`): when the machine states a C travel and no C rate, a C-section rapid that turns C is refused (\"a C-axis rapid that turns C, but the machine file states a C travel but no C rate - its feed would be uncapped; state the C axis's speeds\"). This is the backstop for a stream that bypasses the gate, and it also covers C-turning link rapids that are not orbits, which had the same unbounded F. Cut moves are unchanged: they post at the planned feed.\n\nDecision (named refusal over a stated default rate): `docs/decisions/906-c-unwind-rate-cap.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\n- A machine with C travel and no rate, Rotary Contour on the c_axis_unwind bar: refused at generation by name. The same machine with a travel wide enough for no rewind: generates.\n- The unwound two-ring path posted on that machine: the lathe post refuses by name. The same path on the rated bench posts with no warnings (golden unchanged).\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `c_axis_unwind::a_stated_c_travel_without_a_c_rate_refuses_the_rewind_by_name` (generation, end to end through `operation::generate`)\n- `c_axis_unwind::the_lathe_post_refuses_a_c_turning_rapid_without_a_stated_c_rate` (through the lathe post)\n- `operation::rotary_gate::tests::a_rewind_without_a_stated_c_rate_is_refused_by_name` (gate unit: refused unrated, unwinds rated)\n\n## How tested\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green (app lib, c_axis_fixture, c_axis_live, c_axis_unwind). The first run failed on my own new unit test's fixture (its link chord crossed the spindle line); the fixture was fixed, second run green.\n- Also run: app `lathe_post` 7/7, `lathe_post_refusals` 6/6, `posting` 17/17, `golden_cl` 25/25.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- No NC golden, CL golden or snapshot PNG moved.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A machine that states no C travel and no C rate still posts C-turning rapids uncapped (the `c_axis_live` bench). That predates #860 and is outside this issue; noted in the decision file.\n- `fanuc.cps` / `doosan-dnm.cps` carry no C-rate cap at all (already a known follow-up from #860).\n- Batch and release tiers, ui suites, GUI.\n\nChangelog: A machine file that states a C travel but no C rate now refuses the C rewind (and any C-turning rapid in the lathe post) by name, instead of posting an uncapped feed.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFork synced at v0.17.0.\n\nFixes #906\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
